WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.509
Please welcome Mr. Rory Scovel!

2
00:00:02.509 --> 00:00:06.759
(audience applauding and cheering)

3
00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:43.350
Wow.

4
00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.230
Lotta people are like, "Should we know him?"

5
00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:46.850
Yeah.

6
00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:48.830
You took the longest time...

7
00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:51.550
We've had presidents on the show

8
00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:53.330
that don't take that much time--

9
00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:55.530
Yeah.
to get to their seat.

10
00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:56.650
I don't ever get this,

11
00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:58.999
so I really wanted to soak it up.

12
00:00:58.999 --> 00:01:03.249
(audience applauding and cheering)

13
00:01:07.951 --> 00:01:09.490
You know what's amazing?

14
00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:11.730
You didn't have a beard when you started to walk out here.

15
00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:13.983
No, no.
(laughing)

16
00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:17.300
God, that feels good, thank you, thank you.

17
00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.607
Oh, you son of a bitch.

18
00:01:19.607 --> 00:01:21.450
Thank you.
We got a lot to talk about.

19
00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:22.900
Could it just be this the whole time?

20
00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:24.040
I just keep saying thank you

21
00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:25.690
and people are like, "I like this guy."

22
00:01:25.690 --> 00:01:27.340
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
All right.

23
00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:29.440
There's so much to talk about.

24
00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:32.120
I haven't seen you in a while, and always

25
00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:33.550
you've been one of my favorite stand-up comedians.

26
00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:34.670
You're a hilarious man.
Thank you.

27
00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:37.100
Then, out of the blue, you get the role

28
00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.280
of Amy Schumer's love interest.

29
00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:40.550
Yeah.
How did that happen?

30
00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:45.390
Accomplished actor, they begged, begged me to do it.

31
00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:47.343
You guys know me, I'm in everything.

32
00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:51.767
Literally, it fell from the sky, somebody fell out,

33
00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:54.247
(laughing) couldn't do it, and they were like,

34
00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:57.167
"Who's available and very low priced?"

35
00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:00.430
That's how I basically--

36
00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:02.240
I love the way you sell yourself to a crowd,

37
00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:03.840
I have to say.
(audience laughing)

38
00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:05.628
Well they already applauded for me.

39
00:02:05.628 --> 00:02:07.710
(audience applauding and cheering)

40
00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:08.660
They already applauded, now it's time

41
00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:10.390
for them to know the truth.

42
00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:11.660
So anyway, where were you, where were you?

43
00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:13.330
I was at my house, I was with my daughter.

44
00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:15.360
My wife was gone to do a play for like two weeks.

45
00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:18.563
And I'd just put my daughter down for the night.

46
00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:21.330
Yeah, I got an email from my agent.

47
00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:24.320
He was like, "Read this script, do you wanna do this?"

48
00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:26.020
I'm also like, don't I just say yes?

49
00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:27.640
Am I at the point where I read anything?

50
00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:28.973
Let's just say yes.

51
00:02:30.221 --> 00:02:32.135
You're an automatic yes.

52
00:02:32.135 --> 00:02:33.640
(laughing) Yeah, so I'm reading it,

53
00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:36.170
and I've known Amy through through stand-up for a long time

54
00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:37.097
and she had texted me, she was like,

55
00:02:37.097 --> 00:02:38.370
"It looks like this is gonna happen," I'm like,

56
00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:40.740
I don't even know what's going on, I don't know any of this.

57
00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:42.980
And then three days later, I flew to New York

58
00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:45.663
and we started shooting a film.

59
00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:48.253
I'm in a film.
Yes, you are.

60
00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:52.040
You know, what's funny, well, it's not funny,

61
00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:54.880
but people love your performance, and now you're showing up,

62
00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:57.500
they do, they love your performance.

63
00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:00.330
And I didn't say that was the funny part, but now

64
00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:02.450
these comments come out online,

65
00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:05.350
like this one, this website wrote this about you,

66
00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:07.290
and I think we have it here, Rory Scovel leads

67
00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:11.153
a new generation of sneaky sexy leading men.

68
00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:13.375
And here's the thing,

69
00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:16.560
you know, and when Decider gets the word out

70
00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.730
that means it's gospel.
They're decided.

71
00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:21.340
Yeah, but my question is this:

72
00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:23.430
it feels like a back-handed compliment.

73
00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:25.510
Oh, yeah, yeah.

74
00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:28.080
I love that it's like sneaky-sexy.

75
00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:31.023
It's like, on the outside, no way.

76
00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:33.790
But then we get to know him, and we're like,

77
00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:36.870
maybe there's somethin' to this guy.

78
00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:39.540
Also leads a new generation of sneakies,

79
00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:43.480
I've done one leading romantic love interest thing,

80
00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:46.520
and suddenly, he's leading a generation of men

81
00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:48.310
who are like, six outta 10.

82
00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:50.154
Yeah.
(audience laughing)

83
00:03:50.154 --> 00:03:54.527
That seems new, that's our fearless leader.

84
00:03:54.527 --> 00:03:56.925
Where's our leader, Average Man?

85
00:03:56.925 --> 00:03:58.493
(audience laughing)
I'm here.

